- op: discuss  # 2c2f
  at: '2026-09-21T08:50:14Z'  # 2c2f
  by: agent  # 2c2f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2c2f
  clock: 9  # 2c2f
  nonce: 2c2f  # 2c2f
  message: "STALE `isbefore` REMOVED: WI-togad-gusab-togul-vumaj-habov-vurat-bifut-gohur.\n\nThis row declared that it BLOCKS WI-togad. WI-togad closed `done` on 2026-09-20 -- it shipped ADR-0057 section 14.1 without waiting, because the only two construction sites its finalize step needed (`inherited_calls.py`, 5 sites; `method_call_recovery.py`, 1 site) are exactly the two this row populated the same day. The dependency outlived the thing it was protecting.\n\nWhy it mattered rather than being cosmetic: a blocker pointing at a CLOSED row is a link `ready` can never satisfy and can never clear. It reads to a future agent as \"there is downstream work waiting on the other ~56 files\", which is the opposite of the truth recorded in my 2026-09-20 entry -- the remaining sweep has NO consumer waiting on it, and that is the stated reason it was not done.\n\nNOTHING ELSE CHANGES. Still `todo_hard`, still 2 of ~58 files, still recommended to be driven FROM a second consumer of `derived_from` rather than from the field, so that a wrong site shows up as a wrong demotion instead of as an unverifiable code-reading claim. That recommendation -- and the offer to do the ~56-file sweep as its own family-split PR if the owner wants it regardless -- is still unanswered."  # 2c2f
